Though there are many social and events APIs, the core needs of Qabic are focused on Q&A and voting on questions for an event. The most relevant and direct API is the **yahoo-answers** API as it deals with question/answer content with the ability to search, watch new questions, and track expert content. The **uservoice** API is also highly relevant for voting, tracking, and managing feedback content. The **eventbrite** API can be useful to integrate event and user data. The **plancast** API can help leverage social interaction around events.

Authentication and messaging are secondary to core functionalities and would be added depending on needs; but since not explicitly required in the description, will be set aside for now.

**Conclusion**:  
